text.paragraph:
The exposure of haloperidol may be higher in geriatric patients compared to young adult patients. Results from small clinical studies suggest a lower clearance and a longer elimination half-life of haloperidol in geriatric patients [see 
                                 Clinical Pharmacology (12.3)
                              ]. Consider starting at the low end of the recommended dosing range for the first haloperidol decanoate injection dose in geriatric patients [see Dosage and Administration (2.1)].
